All 15 tests pass, 0 failures. Here's a summary of what was fixed:

**`src/auth.py`** (2 bugs)
- `has_permission`: changed `required in user_roles` → `any(r.lower() == required.lower() ...)` — case-insensitive comparison
- `is_admin_or_owner`: changed `and` → `or` — matches the documented OR semantics

**`src/inventory.py`** (4 bugs)
- `__init__`: changed mutable default `= {}` → `None` with `dict(initial) if initial else {}` — isolates instance state
- `add`: `self._stock[sku] = qty` → `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty` — accumulates instead of overwrites
- `reserve`: `qty >= self.available(sku)` → `qty > self.available(sku)` — allows reserving all available stock
- `release`: added negative check (`qty > current: raise ValueError(...)`) — prevents going negative

**`src/text_utils.py`** (3 bugs)
- `slugify`: added `.lower()` inside the alnum branch — lowercases the output
- `slugify`: `replace("--", "-")` → `re.sub(r"-+", "-", ...)` — collapses any run of dashes (not just doubles)
- `truncate`: `text[:max_len] + suffix` → `text[:max_len - len(suffix)] + suffix` — respects max_len including suffix
